{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nPydantic deliberately counts one Agent-visible model turn even when `FallbackModel` tries multiple candidates inside it. The approved RP-01 decision follows maintained-project practice: keep that request budget authoritative and make candidate activity operationally visible as tracing, not as `candidate_requests` in usage. Candidate construction is centralized in `model_classes.build_fallback_model` (`src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:414+`) and `runner.PydanticAIRunner` already records ordered candidate provenance (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:372-465`). This story is purely additive instrumentation: it does NOT change the S2 `_pai_structured` control flow, whose one bounded operation already preserves the bug-895c native-to-prompted fallback (S2 AC-7).\n\n## Approach\nReuse pydantic-ai's own instrumentation rather than a parallel tracer: wrap each already-built concrete candidate model at construction with `pydantic_ai.models.instrumented.InstrumentedModel` (a public `WrapperModel` subclass, present in 1.107.2) configured via `InstrumentationSettings`, so each candidate request emits an OpenTelemetry span nested — through the ambient span context — beneath the existing Agent model-request span. On top of the library span, record rebar attributes: zero-based `order`, provider-qualified model identity, an `outcome` from the closed vocabulary {`returned`,`raised`}, and provider-reported usage only when the SDK response exposes it (else omitted, never inferred). Any error text placed on a `raised` span is passed through the existing `rebar.llm.failure.sanitize_diagnostic` allowlist sanitizer — no prompt, response, credential, endpoint, or unsanitized body.\n\nThe bug-895c native-to-prompted downgrade needs NO code change here: because both the native and the prompted `agent.run` route through the SAME wrapped candidate models, the downgrade is already legible in the trace as the native attempt's span carrying a `raised` outcome (sanitized rejection reason) followed by the prompted attempt's span carrying `returned`. Instrumentation is best-effort: any exception in candidate wrapping or span emission — tracing enabled or disabled, exporter present or absent — is swallowed at the wrapper boundary so the fallback result, `RunUsage`, and the propagated exception/`FallbackExceptionGroup` are identical to tracing-off. Do not alter `FallbackModel` selection, `ProviderSession` lifecycle, `RunUsage`, `UsageLimits`, pricing, JSONL, or the S2 `_pai_structured` control flow. Provider SDK/HTTP retries stay outside this candidate layer and are never inferred.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` — wrap concrete candidate models with `InstrumentedModel`/`WrapperModel` at construction, without changing order or fallback predicates.\n- `src/rebar/llm/tracing.py` — define the bounded rebar candidate-span attributes (`order`, model identity, `outcome` vocabulary, optional usage) and the `InstrumentationSettings` wiring through the existing optional tracing seam, with best-effort swallow.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — thread candidate order/provenance into the wrapper without adding retry policy.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py`, `tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py` — candidate order, outcome, provenance, and usage non-interference.\n- `tests/unit/test_candidate_tracing.py` — new focused module using an in-memory OTel span exporter, plus the lean-import and tracing-ON span-failure contracts.\n\n## Testing\n- Primary 503 then fallback success: one Agent model-request span with two ordered candidate spans (`raised` then `returned`).\n- All candidates fail: one `raised` span per attempted candidate and the existing ordered `FallbackExceptionGroup`, unchanged.\n- Bug-895c downgrade: native attempt span `raised` (sanitized reason) then prompted attempt span `returned`, with no `_pai_structured` change.\n- Secret-canary: spans carry no prompt, response, credential, endpoint secret, or unsanitized body; raised reason routed through `sanitize_diagnostic`.\n- Tracing ENABLED with a span-emission/exporter failure: result, usage, and propagated exception identical to tracing-off (span error swallowed).\n- Tracing disabled: identical result, usage, imports, and exception behavior.\n- Lean-import subprocess: base install without the tracing extra imports and runs with no span dependency error.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fallback candidates wrapped via pydantic-ai `InstrumentedModel`/`WrapperModel` emit one OTel span per attempted candidate, nested beneath the Agent model-request span, ordered zero-based; verified by an in-memory exporter test.\n- [ ] Each candidate span carries provider-qualified model identity and an `outcome` in the closed set {`returned`,`raised`}; verified by attribute assertions.\n- [ ] The answering fallback model is recorded `returned` and each earlier failed candidate `raised`, preserving the existing ordered `FallbackExceptionGroup` and resolution classification; verified by fallback-chain tests.\n- [ ] The S2-preserved bug-895c native-to-prompted fallback is legible as a native attempt `raised` then a prompted attempt `returned`, with no change to the `_pai_structured` control flow; verified by a downgrade trace test.\n- [ ] Candidate spans contain no prompt, response, credential, endpoint secret, or unsanitized exception body, with the raised reason passed through `rebar.llm.failure.sanitize_diagnostic`; verified by secret-canary assertions.\n- [ ] A span-emission or exporter failure while tracing is ENABLED leaves the fallback result, `RunUsage`, and propagated exception identical to tracing-off; verified by a tracing-ON span-failure test.\n- [ ] `_usage`, `UsageLimits`, pricing, and durable usage JSONL are identical with tracing on and off and contain no candidate counter; verified by paired-result assertions.\n- [ ] The base install without the tracing extra imports and runs with no span dependency error; verified by a lean-import subprocess test."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786962503298769001,"uuid":"e0afc90b-706e-4e32-b3a7-c775b42d309a"}